## [#](#github) GitHub

[![github](https://img.shields.io/github/release/chartjs/Chart.js.svg?style=flat-square&maxAge=600)  (opens new window)](https://github.com/chartjs/Chart.js/releases/latest)

You can download the latest version of [Chart.js on GitHub  (opens new window)](https://github.com/chartjs/Chart.js/releases/latest).

If you download or clone the repository, you must [build](/docs/latest/developers/contributing.html#building-and-testing) Chart.js to generate the dist files. Chart.js no longer comes with prebuilt release versions, so an alternative option to downloading the repo is **strongly** advised.
